WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.910
In this video you'll set the logo and colors that every school in your district starts with.

2
00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:18.122
Here's how it works. Whatever you publish here becomes the default look for each school in your district that hasn't published its own branding. If a school has its own, the school's look always wins.

3
00:00:18.623 --> 00:00:32.883
Select Upload Logo. Use a P-N-G, J-P-G, WebP, or S-V-G file under two megabytes, at least two hundred pixels wide and one hundred tall. A transparent P-N-G works best.

4
00:00:33.384 --> 00:00:44.254
Then select Edit Crop to trim it to fit. Drag the box to move it, or drag the corner to resize it, and select Apply Crop. Cropping never changes your original file.

5
00:00:44.755 --> 00:01:00.495
Set a primary color and a secondary color. An accent color is optional. Pick from the swatch, or type a six digit hex code, such as pound sign one six four F four A. Restore F-N-E Colors puts the standard colors back in the boxes.

6
00:01:00.997 --> 00:01:12.857
Use the preview tabs to see how a school in your district will look to an administrator, a teacher, a classroom, a student, and a parent. Make sure your logo and colors are easy to read.

7
00:01:13.358 --> 00:01:21.018
Select Save Draft to keep your work private. A note below the buttons reminds you when you have changes that haven't been published.

8
00:01:21.518 --> 00:01:28.218
When it looks right, select Publish Branding and confirm. The schools using the district default pick it up.

9
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:36.370
Reset to F-N-E Default removes your district branding and goes back to the standard look. It asks you to confirm first.

10
00:01:36.871 --> 00:01:46.001
Your district's name is shown at the top of the page, but it can't be edited here. Email support at Fixer Nation Education dot com to change it.
